"""argus-console: the console menu of the Argus core and probe VMs (DESIGN 14f).

The login shell of the appliance's console account (argus-console-login runs it through sudo) and a
command, `sudo argus-console`, on any host that carries the host tools. Before any key is pressed it
shows what an operator at the console came to see: address, DNS, the web address (core) or the core
it reports to (probe), time sync, disk, pending OS updates and the state of every service. Then the
handful of actions that otherwise end in a search engine: networking (DHCP or static, DNS),
hostname, a connectivity test, service restarts, logs, OS updates, growing the disk, the keyboard
layout, reboot, power off, and a shell for everything else; on the core also the console password
and a Zabbix server restart, on a probe a check-in on demand and the core it talks to.

ONE FILE, TWO REPOSITORIES: this script is kept byte for byte identical in argus-core
(deploy/core/host/argus-console) and argus-probe (deploy/probe-vm/host/argus-console); it tells the
two hosts apart at start (ROLE), and the core's weekly scan fails when the copies drift.

Standard library only; every command runs without a shell. Paths can be rooted elsewhere with
ARGUS_CONSOLE_ROOT and the role forced with ARGUS_CONSOLE_ROLE (the tests do both).
"""
